{
  "//": [
    "Q14 — State × department × month report (multi-CTE)",
    "What it answers: \"For 2025, which (state, department, month) combinations had at least 10 purchases, and which brought in the most revenue?\"",
    "Route:           GET /reports/cube   (params: start, end, min_purchases; every route also takes db=)",
    "Pattern:         multi_cte_reports",
    "Engine:          MongoDB",
    "Think about it:",
    "idx_* reads 374,436 documents through purchase_date_1; noidx_* reads all",
    "1,000,000 with a COLLSCAN. Which is faster at 1m? Why might reading fewer",
    "documents through an index not win? (SQLite had the same trap; did",
    "PostgreSQL?)"
  ],
  "aggregate": "purchases",
  "cursor": {},
  "pipeline": [
    {
      "$match": {
        "purchase_date": {
          "$gte": "{{start:date}}",
          "$lt": "{{end:date}}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$group": {
        "_id": {
          "state_code": "$state_code",
          "department": "$department",
          "month": {
            "$dateToString": {
              "format": "%Y-%m",
              "date": "$purchase_date"
            }
          }
        },
        "num_purchases": {
          "$sum": 1
        },
        "revenue": {
          "$sum": "$amount"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$match": {
        "num_purchases": {
          "$gte": "{{min_purchases}}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$sort": {
        "revenue": -1,
        "_id.state_code": 1,
        "_id.department": 1,
        "_id.month": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "$limit": 50
    },
    {
      "$project": {
        "_id": 0,
        "state_code": "$_id.state_code",
        "department": "$_id.department",
        "month": "$_id.month",
        "num_purchases": 1,
        "revenue": {
          "$round": [
            "$revenue",
            2
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
